From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: use XDG_STATE_HOME for logs

On Linux, logs are runtime state rather than config or data, so per the XDG Base Directory specification they belong under $XDG_STATE_HOME (defaulting to ~/.local/state) instead of the user data dir (#2636). Adds a userStatePath resolved from XDG_STATE_HOME/~/.local/state (with portable-mode and VSCODE_APPSTATE support) and points logsHome at it instead of userDataPath/logs.

